<h2>Where should the filter controls go on the activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">All three use the same controls: event type, date range, and a shortcut for failed sign-ins. Only the placement differs.</p>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Filter row above the table</h3>
      <p>Controls always visible between the intro and the table. Nothing to open; uses the most vertical space.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p>Recent sign-ins and account changes from the last 90 days.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end;margin:12px 0">
            <div><div class="label">Event type</div><input class="mock-input" value="All events" readonly></div>
            <div><div class="label">Date range</div><input class="mock-input" value="Last 90 days" readonly></div>
            <button class="mock-button">Failed sign-ins only</button>
          </div>
          <p style="opacity:.7">Showing 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>"Filter" button that opens a panel</h3>
      <p>One button above the table opens a popover with the controls. Compact, but every filter takes an extra click and the failed sign-in case is hidden.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p>Recent sign-ins and account changes from the last 90 days.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin:12px 0">
            <span style="opacity:.7">Showing 48 events</span>
            <button class="mock-button">Filter</button>
          </div>
          <div style="border:1px solid currentColor;padding:12px;max-width:280px;margin-left:auto;margin-bottom:12px">
            <div class="label">Event type</div><input class="mock-input" value="All events" readonly>
            <div class="label" style="margin-top:8px">Date range</div><input class="mock-input" value="Last 90 days" readonly>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Quick toggle plus compact row, with removable tags</h3>
      <p>Like A, but the failed sign-in shortcut leads, and active filters show as tags you can remove one at a time. Most discoverable for the Security use case; slightly more to build.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p>Recent sign-ins and account changes from the last 90 days.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end;margin:12px 0">
            <button class="mock-button">Show failed sign-ins</button>
            <div><div class="label">Event type</div><input class="mock-input" value="Sign-in failed" readonly></div>
            <div><div class="label">Date range</div><input class="mock-input" value="Last 7 days" readonly></div>
          </div>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin-bottom:8px">
            <span style="border:1px solid currentColor;padding:2px 8px">Sign-in failed &times;</span>
            <span style="border:1px solid currentColor;padding:2px 8px">Last 7 days &times;</span>
          </div>
          <p style="opacity:.7">Showing 3 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
